<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Charles, Prince of Nassau-Usingen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1712">1712</a>–<a href="/years/1775">1775</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Charles of Nassau-Usingen</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Charles was Prince of Nassau-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/usingen">Usingen</a> from 1718. In 1744 he moved his residence from Usingen to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/biebrich-palace">Biebrich Palace</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wiesbaden">Wiesbaden</a>, which grew as his capital. In 1735 he divided the family inheritance with his brother William Henry, who took Nassau-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saarbrucken">Saarbrücken</a>, and he reorganised the administration of his lands.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charles-prince-of-nassau-usingen.jpg" alt="Charles, Prince of Nassau-Usingen" width="150" height="200" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unidentified painter · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:KarelNU.gif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
